<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results and scores of English county championship:</p>
<p>At The Oval: Warwickshire beat Surrey by 5 wickets. Surrey 193 and 144 (J.Ratcliffe 59; A.Donald 6-55), Warwickshire 306 and 34-5.</p>
<p>Warwickshire 23 points, Surrey 4.</p>
<p>At Chester-le-Street: Durham v Hampshire - match abandoned due to a waterlogged pitch.</p>
<p>Durham 3 points, Hampshire 3.</p>
<p>At Uxbridge: Lancashire beat Middlesex by an innings and 53 runs. Middlesex 119 and 245 (J.Kallis 62; P.Martin 5-47, G.Yates 4-89), Lancashire 417-9 declared.</p>
<p>Lancashire 23 points, Middlesex 1.  </p>
<p>At Leicester: Leicestershire v Yorkshire match drawn.</p>
<p>Yorkshire 268 and 309-3 delcared (D.Lehmann 163 not out, M.Moxon</p>
<p>63). Leicestershire 406-8 declared. Leicester 11 points</p>
<p>Yorkshire 8.</p>
<p>At Swansea: Glamorgan beat Gloucestershire by ten wickets.</p>
<p>Glamorgan 400-5 declared and 52-0. Gloucestershire 214 and 233</p>
<p>(D.Cosker 4-87). Glamorgan 24 points Gloucester 3.</p>
<p>At Maidstone: Northamptonshire beat Kent by one wicket. Kent</p>
<p>306 and 99-2 declared. Northamptonshire 84-0 declared and 322-9</p>
<p>(R.Bailey 83, R.Warren 74, D.,Sales 59). Northants 20 points</p>
<p>Kent 3.</p>
</text>
